@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@*
    #251 · THE THREADS PAGE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    THE THREADS (#741 v1) — the same book read the other way round: every entry that names one
    subject, stacked under that name, with the captain's own line drawn between them.

    Moved out of SatchelPanel.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block
    that was in the panel, character for character. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME
    NAME (a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate under its own name, a variable the
    panel's `@if` bound arrives under the name that binding gave it), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the composition splice it straight back where it came from.

    IHandleEvent repeats SatchelPanel's own override, which repeats Map.Sim.cs's: the HUD's refresh
    belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle, and a child that did not repeat it would put an automatic render
    back on every event in here. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules of its own, and its scope is the
    PAGE's own (b-4dqsdx4p75, pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every rule that styled this markup
    goes on matching it.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block came out of a Razor CODE block, and a code
    block is where its first statements are legal. It is outside the fences, so what the composition reads
    is exactly the lines that stood in the panel.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from SatchelPanel.razor ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
                    @* ── #741 v1 · THE THREADS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                       Owner's issue: "nothing collects every note that mentions The Tilt's harbourmaster, or
                       OFFICE OF WORKS… the player who wants the big picture re-reads the whole book and does
                       the string-and-corkboard in their head — which is fine for three entries and hopeless
                       at thirty."

                       So: one heading per name the book has written down MORE THAN ONCE, and under it every
                       entry that wrote it, oldest first. The rows are the notebook's own nodes — the same
                       titles, the same bullets, the same red-line marks — because a second way of drawing an
                       entry would be a second reading of one book.

                       IT CONCLUDES NOTHING. No arrow, no ranking, no "these are related". The stack is the
                       juxtaposition and the juxtaposition is the whole argument; the captain draws the line,
                       with the same pen, and the book keeps no opinion about what it means. *@
                    <div class="satchel-sub">@SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.Blurb</div>

                    @* ── #973 L3 · MONEY &amp; LOVE (owner ruling §12). The detective's two theories, as a
                       filter over the sheets that stack on this page. It never hides a NOTE: the field
                       book's own threads have no tag to be filtered by, and a filter that silently emptied
                       half the page would be the tab lying about what the book holds. Always lands on the
                       whole book, because a filter that survived the lid is a captain opening their own
                       book onto half of it and not being told why. *@
                    <div class="satchel-notes-filter">
                        <button type="button" class="satchel-filter @(_bookTag is null ? "on" : "")"
                                title="Every sheet in the book"
                                @onclick="() => TheThreadsFilterTurnsTo(null)">🎞 every sheet</button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="satchel-filter @(_bookTag == SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Money ? "on" : "")"
                                title="Only the sheets that follow the money"
                                @onclick="() => TheThreadsFilterTurnsTo(SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Money)">
                            💰 @SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Label(SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Money)
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="satchel-filter @(_bookTag == SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Love ? "on" : "")"
                                title="Only the sheets that follow the heart"
                                @onclick="() => TheThreadsFilterTurnsTo(SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Love)">
                            🖤 @SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Label(SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Theory.Love)
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    @* The sheets, stacked by the names they write down — the photograph's four faces are
                       four threads on the day it is handed over. Drawn above the field book's own stacks
                       and in the same shape, because they are the same page answering the same question
                       about two different kinds of paper. *@
                    @if (SheetStacks() is { Count: > 0 } sheetStacks)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-notes">
                            @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Stack stack in sheetStacks)
                            {
                                <div class="thread-head">
                                    <span class="thread-name">@stack.Heading</span>
                                    <span class="thread-count">
                                        @SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.EntriesLabel(stack.Sheets.Count)
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                                @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.HeldMemory.Sheet sheet in stack.Sheets)
                                {
                                    <div class="held-sheet @(sheet.IsStray ? "stray" : "")">
                                        <div class="held-sheet-text">@sheet.Text</div>
                                        <div class="held-sheet-byline">@sheet.BookLine</div>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    <div class="notebook-pen">
                        <button type="button" class="satchel-filter red-pen @(_penInHand ? "on" : "")"
                                title="@(_penInHand ? SpaceSails.Core.CaseThreads.PenInHandHint : SpaceSails.Core.CaseThreads.PenHint)"
                                @onclick="TakeUpTheRedPen">@SpaceSails.Core.CaseThreads.PenLabel</button>
                        <span class="notebook-register">
                            @(_penInHand
                                ? SpaceSails.Core.CaseThreads.ConnectingBlurb
                                : SpaceSails.Core.CaseThreads.ReadingBlurb)
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    @if (_satchelOutcome is { Length: > 0 } stackSaid)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-outcome">@stackSaid</div>
                    }

                    @if (TheBookThreads() is { Count: > 0 } threads)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-notes">
                            @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.SubjectThread stack in threads)
                            {
                                SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.SubjectThread run = stack;
                                <div class="thread-head">
                                    <span class="thread-name">@stack.Heading</span>
                                    <span class="thread-count">
                                        @SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.EntriesLabel(stack.Entries.Count)
                                    </span>
                                    @* The pen, offered where the stack is. Never disabled and never hidden
                                       (#212/#603): pressed on your feet or at a bar top it answers with the
                                       sentence that says what would fix it, exactly as the pen itself does. *@
                                    <button type="button" class="satchel-filter thread-pen"
                                            title="@SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.ConnectTheStackHint"
                                            @onclick="() => RunThePenDownTheStack(run)">
                                        @SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.ConnectTheStackLabel
                                    </button>
                                </div>
                                <NotebookNodes Rows="@NotebookPage(stack.Entries)"
                                               PenInHand="_penInHand"
                                               WithPlace="true"
                                               IsOpen="NodeIsOpen"
                                               IsHeld="NodeIsHeld"
                                               OnTitle="NoteTitlePressed" />
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-empty">@SpaceSails.Core.CaseSubjects.NothingTwiceLine</div>
                    }
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
